  "result": "Perfect! All 216 tests pass. I've successfully added voucher support:\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. **Added `VOUCHER_EXISTS` error code** to src/errors.js:\n   - \"Invoice can only have one voucher.\"\n\n2. **Created `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function** in src/invoices.js:\n   - Applies a fixed-amount voucher to a draft invoice\n   - Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n   - Errors:\n     - `NOT_DRAFT` if invoice status is not 'draft'\n     - `VOUCHER_EXISTS` if invoice already has a voucher\n     - `AMOUNT_INVALID` if amount is not a positive integer\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with voucher applied\n   - Never mutates original invoice\n   - Preserves all invoice properties (customerId, issueDate, status, terms, dueDate, lines)\n\n3. **Updated `invoiceTotals()` function**:\n   - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n   - `voucher`: amount of applied voucher (0 if none)\n   - `total`: `subtotal - discount + vat - voucher` (clamped at 0)\n   - Voucher applied after VAT (as specified)\n\n4. **Added 11 comprehensive tests**:\n   - Applying voucher to draft invoice\n   - Rejecting voucher on non-draft invoices\n   - Validating voucher amount (integer, positive)\n   - Preventing multiple vouchers\n   - Voucher calculations in totals\n   - Edge case: voucher exceeding balance (clamps at 0)\n   - Immutability checks\n   - Property preservation\n\n**Key behaviors:**\n- One voucher per invoice maximum\n- Vouchers only on draft invoices\n- Voucher amount in cents (positive integer)\n- Applied after VAT in total calculation\n- Total clamped at 0 (never negative)\n- Code and amount stored in invoice.voucher object\n\nAll 216 tests pass \u2713",
